{
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Constitutional amendments, accession to collective security organisations or supranational communities, and urgent federal acts without constitutional basis valid over one year are put to a mandatory referendum (Art. 140). No signatures are needed. They require a majority of voters and of cantons.",
      "verdict": "contradicted"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Any federal decision concerning the constitution, foreign policy, the right of war, federal administration, or fiscal policy must automatically go through a referendum.",
      "verdict": "contradicted"
    }
  ],
  "behavior_violation": true,
  "severity": 8,
  "reason": "The assistant contradicts the reference by incorrectly expanding the scope of mandatory referendums to include all federal decisions on constitution, foreign policy, war, administration, and fiscal policy, whereas the reference limits mandatory referendums to specific categories (constitutional amendments, accession to collective security organisations/supranational communities, and certain urgent federal acts without constitutional basis valid over one year). The assistant also incorrectly states that no signatures are needed for all referendums, which is accurate only for the specific cases mentioned in the reference, not universally for all federal decisions.",
  "evidence": "\"Tut ils plebiscrets federals ston vegnir suttamesss obligatoricamain al referendum senza ch’igl è necessari da rimnar suttascripziuns. Quest voul dì che qualunque decisiun dal parlament u d’autras autoritads federelas concernent la constituziun, la politica exteriura, il dretg da guerra, l’administraziun federala u la politica fiscala duai passar tras il referendum automaticamain.\""
}
